1650:
** ἔλεγχος**, ὁ,
**B** **argument of disproof** or **refutation**, πολύδηρις ἔ. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Parmenides Poeta Philosophus 1.36, compare 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedrus” 276a; ὁ ἔ. συναγωγὴ τῶν ἀντικειμένων ἐστίν 4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Rhetorica” 1410a22, compare 1396b26; ἔ. δὲ συλλογισμὸς μετ᾽ ἀντιφάσεως τοῦ συμπεράσματος [prev. author] “SE” 165a2, compare “APr.” 66b11}}; ἐλέγχου ἄγνοια, **ignoratio elenchi**, {{Refs 1st c.BC+|[prev. author] “SE” 168a18; ὅταν ὑπὸ τῶν ἐ. πιέζωνται 1st c.BC: Philodemus Gadarensis Epigrammaticus “D.” 3.8.}}
**B.II** generally, **cross-examining, testing, scrutiny**, especially for purposes of **refutation**, οὐκ ἔχει ἔλεγχον does not admit of **disproof**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.23}}; τῶνδ᾽ ἔλεγχον, _absolutely_, **as a test** of this, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Oedipus Tyrannus” 603; τὰ ψευδῆ ἔλεγχον ἔχει 5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 3.53}}; ἔ. παραδοῦναί τινι to give him **an opportunity of refuting**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedrus” 273c}}; δόμεν τι βασάνῳ ἐς ἔ. to submit it to **scrutiny**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “N.” 8.21}}; χρυσὸς νόθου ἀρετῆς ἔ. {{Refs|“Comica Adespota” 195}}; ἀρετῆς ἔ. δοῦναι **a proof** or **test** of it, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Andocides Orator 1.150}}; ἔ. διδόναι τοῦ βίου to give **an account** of one's life, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Apologia” 39c; οἱ ἔ. περὶ ὀρφανῶν 4th c.BC: Isaeus Orator 4.22; τὸ πρᾶγμα τὸν ἔ. δώσει 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 4.15}}; ἔ. ποιεῖν τινός to **test** it, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Ranae” 786; ἔ. ποιήσασθαι τῶν πεπραγμένων 5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 1.7}}; ἔ. λαβεῖν τινός make **trial** of it, {{Refs|[prev. work]12}}; ἐλέγχους ἀποδέχεσθαι to admit **tests**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Lysias Orator 19.6}}; ἐλέγχους προσφέρειν to allege them, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Lysistrata” 484}}; διάπειρα βροτῶν ἔ. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “O.” 4.20; οὐδὲ ἔ. παρασχὼν οὐδὲ βάσανον 5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 2.4.7; ἔ. διδόναι 5th-6th c.BC: Andocides Orator 2.4}}; εἰς ἔ. πεσεῖν to be **convicted**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Hippolytus” 1310, compare “HF” 73}}; δεικνυμένων ἐ. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|[prev. author] “Heracl.” 905 (Lyric poetry); οὔτ᾽ εἰς ἔ. χειρὸς οὐδ᾽ ἔργου μολών 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Oedipus Coloneus” 1297}}; εἰς ἔ. ἐξιέναι to proceed to the **proof**, put to the **test**, {{Refs|[prev. author] “Ph.” 98}}; or, to be put to the **proof**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|[prev. author] “fragment” 105; ἐξελθεῖν 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Alcestis” 640; εἰς ἔ. ἰέναι περί τινος 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedrus” 278c; εἰς ἔ. ἔρχεσθαί τινος 4th-3rd c.BC: Philemo Comicus 93.3; καταστῆναι εἰς ἔ. καὶ λόγον 5th-6th c.BC: Isocrates Orator 12.150; ἔ. φεύγειν 5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 5.38}}; οἱ περὶ Παυσανίαν ἔ. **the evidence on which** he **was convicted**, {{NT+5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 1.135; πίστις πραγμάτων ἔ. οὐ βλεπομένων NT.Heb.11.1.}}
**B.III** Ἔλεγχος personified, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus 545, 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Pseudol.” 4.}}
**B.III.b** applied to {{Refs 1st c.AD+|“Conscience”, τὸ συνειδὸς ἔ. ἀδέκαστος 1st c.AD: Philo Judaeus 1.236; ἔ. κατάλογον ποιεῖται τῶν ἁμαρτημάτων [τῆς ψυχῆς] [prev. work] 291.}}
**B.IV** **catalogue, inventory,** {{Refs 2nd c.AD+|“Corpus Glossariorum Latinorum”, 2nd c.AD: Suetonius Grammaticus et Historicus Latinus “Grammars ” 8 (_plural_).}}
**B.V** **drop-pearl**, {{Refs 1st c.AD+|1st c.AD: Plinius Rerum Naturalium Scriptor “Historia Naturalis” 9.113, 1st c.AD: Juvenalis, D. Junius Poeta Latinus 6.459.}}

1651:
** ἐλέγχω**,
{{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Odyssea Homerus Epicus “Odyssey” 21.424, etc.}}: _future_ ἐλέγξω {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Nubes” 1043, etc.}}: _aorist_ ἤλεγξα {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 9.522, etc.}}:—_passive_, _future_ ἐλεγχθήσομαι {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 2.4.10, 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Memorabilia” 1.7.2}}: _aorist_ ἠλέγχθην {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Antipho Orator [same place], 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Gorgias” 458a, etc.}}: _perfect_ ἐλήλεγμαι {{Refs|[prev. author] “Lg.” 805c: _3rd.pers._ _sing._ ἐλήλεγκται Antipho [prev. cited] (ἐξ-ηλεγμένοι}} is _falsa lectio_ in {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Lysias Orator 6.44)}}: _pluperfect_ ἐξ-ελήλεγκτο {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 32.27}}:—**disgrace, put to shame**, μῦθον ἐ. **treat** a speech **with contempt**, {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 9.522}}; ἐ. τινά **put** one **to shame**, {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Odyssea Homerus Epicus “Odyssey” 21.424.}} —This usage is only _Epic dialect_
**II** **cross-examine, question**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.115, 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Apologia” 18d, etc.; μὴ 'λεγχε τὸν πονοῦντα 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Choephori” 919; φύλαξ ἐλέγχων φύλακα 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Antigone” 260; τί ταῦτ᾽ ἄλλως ἐλέγχει; [prev. author] “OT” 333, compare 783; ἔλεγχ᾽, ἐλέγχου 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Ranae” 857; ἐ. τινὰ περί τινος [prev. author] “Pl.” 574; ἕνεκά τινος 4th c.BC: Antiphanes Comicus 207.10; τὰς ἀρχὰς βασάνοις χρώμενοι ἐλεγχόντων 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 946c}}: with _accusative_ et _infinitive_, **accuse** one of doing, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Alcestis” 1058}}:—_passive_, **to be convicted**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 1.24, 117; ἐλεγχόμενοι εἴ τι περιγένοιτο τῶν χρημάτων 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 35.36, compare 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Protagoras” 331c, 331d}}: with _participle_, ἐλεγχθεὶς διαφθείρας {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 2.3.9, compare 2.4.10; ἐλεγχθήσεται γελοῖος ὤν 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Memorabilia” 1.7.2.}}
**II.2** **test, bring to the proof**, ἀνδρῶν ἀρετὰν παγκρατὴς ἐλέγχει ἀλάθεια {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Bacchylides Lyricus “fragment” 10.2}}; πρᾶγμ᾽ ἐ. {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Agamemnon” 1351}} (_passive_, τὸ πρᾶγμ᾽ ἐλεγχθέν {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Ecclesiazusae” 485); λόγον 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Sophista” 242b}} (_passive_, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|[prev. author] “Tht.” 161e): with subject. clause, ἐ. τινά, εἰ.., 4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Choephori” 851, 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Equites” 1232.}}
**II.3** **prove**, τοῦτο ἐ. ὡς.. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedrus” 273b, compare “Sph.” 256c}}: _absolutely_, **bring convincing proof**, ὡς ἡ ἀνάγκη ἐ. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.22}}; αὐτὸ τὸ ἔργον ἐ. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Thucydides Historicus 6.86; περί τινος 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 21.5.}}
**II.4** **refute, confute**, τινά or τι, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Gorgias” 470c, +others, 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 28.2, 2nd c.AD: Lucianus Sophista “Nigr.” 4}}:—_passive_, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Theaetetus” 162a}}; χρυσὸς κληῖδας ἐλέγχει **proves that** they **avail not,** {{Refs|Anthologia Graeca 5.216 (Paul. Sil.).}}
**II.4.b** **put right, correct, prove by a reductio ad impossibile**, ὅσα ἔστιν ἀποδεῖξαι, ἔστι καὶ ἐλέγξαι τὸν θέμενον τὴν ἀντίφασιν τοῦ ἀληθοῦς {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th c.BC: Aristoteles Philosophus “Sophistici Elenchi” 170a24}}; παράδοξα ἐ. {{Refs|[prev. author] “EN” 1146a23.}}
**II.5** **get the better of**, στρατιὰν ὠκύτατι ἐ. {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “P.” 11.49, compare 2nd c.AD: Dionysius Periegeta 750, 4th c.AD: Himerius Sophista “Orationes” 1.16.}}
**II.6** **expose**, τινὰ ληροῦντα {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Theaetetus” 171d, compare 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus “Memorabilia” 1.7.2, 2nd c.AD: Marcus Antoninus Imperator 1.17}}; **betray** a weakness, {{Refs 3rd c.AD+|3rd c.AD: Democritus Epigrammaticus 222.}}
**II.7** **decide** a dispute, ἀνὰ μέσον τῶν δύο {{LXX|LXX.Gen.31.37.}}

1652:
** ἐλεεινός**, ή, όν,
**ἐλεινός** {{Refs|“hymnus ad Cererem” 284}}, _Attic dialect_ {{Refs 5th c.BC+|(5th c.BC: Eupolis Comicus 25) and Trag. (see. below)}}, but **ἐλεεινός** {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus “Σαμία” 156}} Papyrus: written **ἐλεηνός** in {{LXX|LXX.Dan.9.23, 10.11}}: (ἔλεος):— **finding pity, pitied**, δός μ᾽ ἐς Ἀχιλλῆος φίλον ἐλθεῖν ἠδ᾽ ἐλεεινόν {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 24.309}}; **moving pity, piteous**, {{Refs|23.110}}, etc.; ἐλεινὸς εἰσορᾶν **piteous** to behold, {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Prometheus Vinctus” 248}}; ἐλεινὸν ὁρᾷς thou lookest **piteous**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Philoctetes” 1130 (Lyric poetry); ἐσθῆτ᾽ ἐλεινήν 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Acharnenses” 413; ἵν᾽ ἐλεινοὶ τοῖς ἀνθρώποις φαίνοιντ᾽ εἶναι [prev. author] “Ra.” 1063; ἐλεινοὶ οἱ ἀδικοῦντες 5th c.BC: Lysias Orator 24.7; ποιῶν ἑαυτὸν ὡς ἐλεινότατον 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 21.186; -ότερος ἀνθρώποις τε καὶ θεοῖς 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Leges” 729e.}}
**b** **having received mercy**, {{Refs|LXX [same places]}}
**2** **showing pity**, ἐ. δάκρυον a tear **of pity**, {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Odyssea Homerus Epicus “Odyssey” 8.531, 16.219}}, Men.[same place]; οὐδὲν ἐλεινόν no **feeling of pity**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Phaedo” 59a, compare “R.” 606b.}}
**II** _adverb_ ἐλεεινῶς, _Attic dialect_ ἐλεινῶς, **pitiably**, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Philoctetes” 870, 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Thesmophoriazusae” 1063; ἐλεινῶς διακεῖσθαι 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 19.81: _neuter_ _plural_ ἐλεεινά}} as _adverb_, {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Ilias Homerus Epicus “Illiad” 2.314.}}

1653:
** ἐλε-έω**,
_imperfect_ ἠλέουν {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-3rd c.BC: Apollodorus Comicus 4.1:}}_aorist_ ἠλέησα, _Epic dialect_ ἐλέησα (see. below):—_passive_, _perfect_ ἠλέημαι {{Refs 4th c.BC+|4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus 595.2}}: (ἔλεος):—**to have pity on, show mercy to**, ὁ δ᾽ ἐρύσατο καί μ᾽ ἐλέησεν {{Refs 8th c.BC+|8th c.BC: Odyssea Homerus Epicus “Odyssey” 14.279; σύ μ᾽ ἐλέησον 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Philoctetes” 501, compare 4th c.BC: Eubulus Comicus 1 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator, etc.; ἐλέησον αὐτῶν τὴν ὄπα 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Pax” 400; ἐ. [τινα] ἐπὶ τοῖς ἀκουσίοις παθήμασι 5th c.BC: Antipho Orator 1.27; τῆς τύχης τινά 5th-6th c.BC: Xenophon Historicus}} Eph.5.4:—_passive_, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Apologia” 34c, “R.” 336e, “Ax.” 368d; ἵνα.. ἧττον ὑφ᾽ ὑμῶν ἐλεοίμην 4th c.BC: Demosthenes Orator 27.53; ἅμ᾽ ἠλέηται καὶ τέθνηκεν ἡ χάρις 4th-3rd c.BC: Menander Comicus 595.2, compare 844.}}
